2:T1186,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"BlogPosting","@id":"https://www.melius.com/blog/best-tools-ai-generated-design-concepts#article","headline":"Best tools for AI generated design concepts","description":"Five AI tools for generating design concepts, compared on how precisely you can set a direction, comparing options, and reusing a look later.","url":"https://www.melius.com/blog/best-tools-ai-generated-design-concepts","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.melius.com/blog/best-tools-ai-generated-design-concepts"},"datePublished":"2026-09-05","dateModified":"2026-09-05","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Melius Team","url":"https://www.melius.com"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://www.melius.com/#organization"},"isPartOf":{"@id":"https://www.melius.com/#website"},"inLanguage":"en-US","image":"https://www.melius.com/images/blog/best-tools-ai-generated-design-concepts/cover.webp","timeRequired":"PT10M","wordCount":1914,"articleSection":"Comparisons","keywords":"Comparisons"},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Blog","item":"https://www.melius.com/blog"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Best tools for AI generated design concepts","item":"https://www.melius.com/blog/best-tools-ai-generated-design-concepts"}]},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the best AI tool for design concepts?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Match it to the discipline: Midjourney for the loosest visual exploration, Vizcom for physical product concepts from sketches, Recraft for identity and vector systems, and Melius when the approved direction has to be reapplied across a body of work. Kosmik is the one to add if your problem is research and not generation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can AI generate design concepts that are actually usable?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes at the direction stage, less so as finished work. These tools are strong at proposing and resolving a look and weak at the precision a production asset needs, so the realistic use is to settle the direction with AI and finish in your normal tools. Treat the output as a concept, which is what it's good at."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I keep a concept consistent once it's approved?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Capture the direction as something reusable instead of one image. A written style description, a saved style, or a brand kit can all be reapplied months later; a single lucky generation cannot. On Melius the approved direction stays as a node you re-run against new inputs, which is the same idea made concrete."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Midjourney still the best for concept art?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For range and aesthetic quality it's still the one most designers reach for first, and style references have made it much more directable. Its weaknesses are everything after the idea: brand control, legible text, exact palettes and getting a look out of Midjourney and into real assets. There's also no free tier, so you can't test it against your references before paying."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need to be able to draw to use AI concepting tools?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No for graphic and brand concepting, and it helps a lot for product concepting. Vizcom is built around a sketch and rewards being able to make one, while the others take a written direction or a reference set. If you can't draw, working from references instead of from a blank prompt gets you much closer."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I own concepts I generate with AI?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It varies by tool, so check before a concept goes into client work. On Melius you own what you create and can use it commercially, subject to the underlying model providers' terms, and Melius does not use your work to train AI models. Read the terms per tool, because free consumer tiers are the ones most likely to restrict commercial use."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Will AI concepting replace art direction?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Generating options is now nearly free, which makes choosing between them the scarce skill and no longer the easy part. The judgment about which direction is right for this brand and this audience is the work, and these tools remove the labour around that decision, not the decision itself."}}]}]}7:X
